*, size_t, int, uint32_t)` |\n\n**Missing symbols: none.** `nm -D` diff between the two libraries is empty:\n\n```\ndiff <(nm -D --defined-only c_so/libcstrfun.so       | awk '{print $NF}' | sort) \\\n     <(nm -D --defined-only target/release/libdriver.so | awk '{print $NF}' | sort)\n```\n\nUndefined (imported) symbols of the Rust `.so` are libc/`ld` runtime symbols\nonly (`memcpy`, `__libc_start_main`, `pthread_*`, …); no non-libc symbol is\nleft undefined.\n\n## Executable surface\n\n`c_src/src/main.c` is a `main()` that reads a fixed token stream from stdin and\nprints the `process_strings` result, so its whole observable surface is\nstdin → (stdout, stderr, exit status). It is translated by `src/main.rs`\n(+ `src/scanf.rs` for the `scanf` conversions and `src/mem.rs`/`src/frame_junk.rs`\nfor the `main` stack frame the C code reads past the end of its buffers into).\nIt is verified with the executable-level differential tests in\n`tests/exe_diff.rs`, which run the real C binary and the real Rust binary.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":131762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":495,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15f0aaf7-a9d4-460c-89ca-e65368d5a4d2","uuid":"fe196287-6026-4054-99b0-a08e12e458e5","timestamp":"2026-08-20T00:19:45.557Z"}
